;; closure-folds.edn — structured fold records (input to cascade_learn.py / Build 2).
;; Each record: which LIBRARY patterns actually folded the hole (the graph-rewrite rules
;; applied), extracted from futon6/holes/early-closures.md. `used` = the subset of the
;; cascade whose THEN-clauses did the fold; `success` = did it fold. This is the dense,
;; real, peradam-free learning signal (pattern-utility + co-usage for edge-seeding).
;;
;; RECORDING DISCIPLINE (claude-1, 2026-06-10 — the β / discrimination unlock): record FAILED folds too.
;; The signal is only dense if BOTH outcomes are written. Today this file is survivorship-biased (5
;; success, 0 failure) → every posterior can only go UP (β can't grow), so the grounded A/B is stuck at
;; the uniform-0.667 ceiling. When a fold-attempt's `:used` set does NOT close its hole, write a record
;; with `:success false` + that `:used` (+ evidence of the attempt). That recorded NEGATIVE is the β
;; term — the amortization principle ("if no, we still learned something") made data. cascade_learn
;; already consumes `:success false` (used-and-didn't-close → β+=1; failed pairs never seed an edge).
[{:scope "recommendation-bindings/q5" :used [] :success true :note "investigation closure, no fold"}
